=== cech
cech is the command-line tool of CECH, a marketplace of agent skills

Usage:
  cech [command]

Available Commands:
  build       write the files generated from a marketplace's sources
  completion  print the completion script of a shell
  help        print the help of cech or of a command
  version     print the version of cech

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for cech

Use "cech [command] --help" for more information about a command.
=== cech build
Write the files generated from the hand-written sources of a
marketplace with CECH's layout: the catalogue
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json, Codex TOML for each reviewer agent, a
copy of the root LICENSE in each skill folder, .github/CODEOWNERS and
docs/catalogue.md. In each plugin.json it sets the description, the
version and, in an extension, each CECH dependency's marketplace. It
prints each file it creates, updates or removes.

Usage:
  cech build [flags]

Flags:
      --check              write nothing; list each file that differs from what the build would write, and fail if there is one
  -C, --directory string   run in this directory, the marketplace's root, instead of the current one (default ".")
      --dry-run            write nothing, and list the files the build would change
  -h, --help               help for build
      --json               print one JSON object with the mode, whether it passed, the files, any changes a failed build did not make, and any errors
      --release string     build this release, as X.Y.Z or X.Y.Z-rc.N: the catalogue is named after the namespace and the release, and every plugin's version is the release; without it, the version is 0.0.0-dev
=== cech completion
Print the completion script of a shell, for the shell to source.
Run cech completion <shell> --help for how to load it.

Usage:
  cech completion [command]

Available Commands:
  bash        print the completion script of bash
  fish        print the completion script of fish
  powershell  print the completion script of powershell
  zsh         print the completion script of zsh

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for completion

Use "cech completion [command] --help" for more information about a command.
=== cech help
Print the help of cech, or of the command named, as cech help completion bash.

Usage:
  cech help [command] [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for help
=== cech version
Print the version of cech.

Usage:
  cech version [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for version
      --json   print one JSON object with the version, the Go release that built cech, and the OS and architecture it was built for
